---
title: Vegan Lasagna
portions: 8
category: Pasta
source: "https://www.lovingitvegan.com/vegan-lasagna/"
---

## Bolognese

[Process] Slice the @mushrooms{180 g} and process in a #food processor{} until very finely chopped. Add to a #mixing bowl{}. Crumble in the @tofu{224 g}(extra-firm) and add the @walnuts{70 g}(processed into crumbs). Mix together.

[Sauté] Add the @onion{55 g}(chopped) to a #pot{} with the @garlic{15 ml}(crushed), the @olive-oil{15 ml}, the @oregano-dried{2 g}, the @basil{1 g}(dried) and the @cayenne-pepper{0.5 g} and sauté until softened, ~{3 min}.

[Braise] Add the mushroom mix, the @soy-sauce{15 ml}(dark), the @tomato-paste{120 g} and the @marinara-sauce{240 g}. Sauté until you have a soft bolognese with no visible liquid. Balance with the @sugar{12 g}(coconut) and season with @salt{} and @black-pepper{}.

## Cheese sauce

[Roux] Heat the @olive-oil{90 ml} in a #pot{}. Add the @flour{40 g} and fry briefly, stirring vigorously. Pour in all of the @soy-milk{960 ml}, whisking to remove lumps.

[Thicken] Bring to the boil stirring constantly and let it boil until thickened, ~{3 min}. Off heat, stir in the @dijon-mustard{30 ml}, the @nutritional-yeast{25 g}, the @onion-powder{3 g}, the @garlic-powder{3 g}, the @paprika{1 g}(smoked), the @salt{3 g} and the @black-pepper{2 g}.

## Assemble

[Preheat] Preheat the #oven{} to ^{200°C}.

[Layer] In a deep 9×13 #baking dish{}, layer: thin layer of @marinara-sauce{}, 4 @lasagna-sheets{}, half the bolognese spread evenly, thin layer of cheese sauce, sliced @zucchini{}(4 small), all of the @vegan-ricotta{400 g}, then repeat: 4 @lasagna-sheets{}, more @marinara-sauce{}, thin layer of cheese sauce, remaining bolognese, sliced @zucchini{}, final 4 @lasagna-sheets{} and remaining @marinara-sauce{}.

[Bake covered] Cover with foil and bake, ~{30 min}.

[Bake open] Remove foil, pour the rest of the cheese sauce on top and return to the #oven{} uncovered, ~{20 min}.

## Serve

[Rest] Test with a knife that the sheets are cooked through. Drizzle the middle with marinara and decorate with chopped @basil{} and ground @black-pepper{}.
